# HCOS™ Decision Checklist

## Purpose

Use this checklist before finalizing significant decisions, implementing organizational changes, reviewing incidents, adopting technologies, or approving governance actions.

## Decision Classification

### Decision Type

- [ ] Strategic
- [ ] Operational
- [ ] Clinical
- [ ] AI Governance
- [ ] Financial
- [ ] Policy
- [ ] Human Resources
- [ ] Technology
- [ ] Quality Improvement
- [ ] Other: ______________________

### Decision Impact

- [ ] Low
- [ ] Moderate
- [ ] High
- [ ] Critical

### Review Level

- [ ] Individual
- [ ] Team
- [ ] Leadership
- [ ] Executive
- [ ] Governing Body

## HCOS™ Decision Pattern

```text
Understand Before You Judge
✓ Purpose
✓ Analysis
↓
Assign Responsibility Fairly
✓ Accountability
↓
Strengthen the System
✓ Stewardship
✓ Transparency
✓ Continuous Learning
```

# 1. Understand

## Purpose

- [ ] Is the purpose clearly defined?
- [ ] Does the decision support the organization's mission and values?
- [ ] Have we identified who may be affected?
- [ ] Have we considered short- and long-term impacts?

## Analysis

- [ ] Do we understand what happened?
- [ ] Have we separated evidence from assumptions?
- [ ] Have we identified uncertainty?
- [ ] Have we considered system factors?
- [ ] Have we gathered appropriate perspectives?
- [ ] Have we considered unintended consequences?

# 2. Assign Responsibility Fairly

## Accountability

- [ ] Is decision-making authority clearly identified?
- [ ] Do responsibilities match authority?
- [ ] Were adequate resources available?
- [ ] Were expectations reasonable?
- [ ] Has accountability been communicated?
- [ ] Have implementation responsibilities been assigned?

# 3. Strengthen the System

## Stewardship

- [ ] Have we identified opportunities for improvement?
- [ ] Have we considered what should remain unchanged?
- [ ] Have we preserved valuable knowledge?
- [ ] Have we documented the rationale?
- [ ] Have we identified how success will be monitored?

## Transparency

- [ ] Could someone unfamiliar with the decision understand why it was made?
- [ ] Is supporting evidence documented?
- [ ] Are assumptions identified?
- [ ] Is the reasoning transparent?
- [ ] Can the decision be reviewed later?

## Continuous Learning

- [ ] What have we learned?
- [ ] What should improve?
- [ ] What should be preserved?
- [ ] What should future leaders inherit?
- [ ] When will this decision be reviewed?

## Final Reflection

- Have we sought understanding before judgment?
- Does accountability match authority?
- Does this decision respect human dignity?
- Have affected perspectives been considered?
- Does this decision strengthen trust?
- Will future leaders understand why it was made?

